Specifications
--------------

RFC 792 / RFC 4443 / RFC 1071 (echo codec + checksum), `ip(7)` / `ipv6(7)`
(socket options, `IP_PKTINFO`/`IPV6_PKTINFO`).

Design reference — fping
------------------------

fping (schweikert/fping, **Stanford BSD-with-advertising**).

The paced ping engine (`pinger.zig`) follows fping's main-loop DESIGN — two
time-ordered event queues, timeouts serviced first, a global minimum send
interval, per-host cadence scheduled off nominal event time, retry with
timeout backoff — and adopts fping's default timing constants (10 ms global
interval, 1000 ms per-host, 500 ms timeout, 3 retries, 1.5 backoff).

NO fping source was copied: the expression is independent throughout (binary
heaps vs fping's intrusive linked lists, a hard in-flight cap, per-subnet send
spacing, first-probe jitter, `sendmmsg` batching, `ppoll` vs `select`, lazy vs
eager purge of answered timeout events), no C statement sequence and no comment
text survives, and this is a library with a callback API rather than a CLI's
main loop.

The `--oiface` `IP_PKTINFO`/`ipi_spec_dst` construction in `Socket.zig` was
cross-checked against fping's `socket4.c` behavior.

Recorded because architecture and functional default values are not
copyrightable expression (17 USC 102(b): procedure, process, system, method of
operation) — this is a provenance record, not an attribution obligation, and
fping's advertising clause does not reach it.
